## Group a of the small acts at the hearts of places: craft (PlaceDeeds;
## the contract is written at the top of place_deeds.gd).
##
## Five acts: forge-nail, caulk-seam, proof-the-block, rope-right-angle
## and prune-vine.  Each is a short chain of steps where the order or the
## discernment of the craft matters.  A wrong step answers in the craft's
## own language (TABOO 0.39: the smith speaks of iron and heat, the
## shipwright of flax and tar) and leaves the step open; the right step
## moves on; the last one closes the act with what it taught.  Nothing
## is random, nothing changes FORM, nothing is counted as a reward: the
## state is only {step, reply, done}.  No act here asks to wait, so
## tick() leaves the state as it was.
##
## Constitution: ФОРМА (the place and its craft) → ДЕЙСТВИЕ (the work done
## in its right order) → ЦЕЛЬ (the lesson of the place held in the hands).
extends RefCounted

## Every step is {"q": the question of the panel, "o": [option, ...]};
## an option is [id, button text, is it right, reply].  The right options
## stand at different places in the lists (the first or the second, so
## that the shared walker of tests/test_place_deeds.gd, which tries the
## first buttons in turn, always reaches it).  No button carries a church
## word (TABOO 0.39 item 3); the scripture of a place stands only in its closing reply.
